 # Raw Volume Data Reader
 
-Also called: 3D Raw Volume Texture Loading, BrickDensityRegion Volume Slice Loading, Raw CT Data Loading, Raw Volume Data Loading, RawReader, Volume Data Loading
+Also called: Raw Volume Data Loading, Raw Volume File Loading, Volume Data I/O (Raw), RawReader
 
 ## Overview
-The Raw Volume Data Reader loads raw binary volume data into memory, parsing dimensions and converting high-precision integer values (typically 8-bit or 16-bit) into normalized floats or GPU-compatible textures [S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, S7, S8, S9, unofficial]. It solves the problem of transferring large, high-bit-depth medical imaging datasets (such as CT scans) into the graphics pipeline by providing a direct, format-agnostic binary interface [S2, S3, S4, S7, unofficial]. Unlike structured metadata parsers like [HDF5 JSON (H5J) File Parsing](2922-hdf5-json-h5j-file-parsing.md), it operates directly on raw binary slices without intermediate schema interpretation, serving as the foundation for subsequent bit-depth reduction and normalization steps [S1, S3, S10, unofficial].
+The Raw Volume Data Reader loads raw binary volume data into memory, parsing dimensions and converting high-precision integer values (typically 8-bit or 16-bit) into normalized floats or GPU-compatible textures [S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, S7, S8, S9, S10, unofficial]. It solves the problem of transferring volumetric datasets into the graphics pipeline by providing a direct binary interface [S2, S3, S4, S7, unofficial].
 
