 ## Background
-The Raw Volume Data Reader is a fundamental method in volume rendering, originating from the need to load raw binary data from CT scanners and other imaging devices directly into graphics pipelines [S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, S7, S8, S9, S10, unofficial][S11]. It is widely used in research prototypes and custom rendering engines where simplicity and performance are prioritized over format compatibility [S1, S2, S3, S7, S8, S9, S10, unofficial]. Variants have been developed to handle specific challenges like endianness, metadata parsing, and 2D stream processing [S9, S10, unofficial][S11].
